-- title:
--   Descent of the mod-p weight condition along algebraic extensions
-- statement:
--   Let $K_0$ and $K$ be fields with $K$ a $K_0$-algebra that is algebraic over $K_0$, let $m$ be a natural number, and let $G$ be a Laurent series over $K_0$ (a Hahn series on $\mathbb{Z}$ with coefficients in $K_0$). Write $\bar j_F$ for the element `jqModC` of $F((q))$ attached to a field $F$, namely $q^{-1}$ times the image over $F$ of the integral power series `jNum`, and recall that `IsModPFormFn F m H` asserts two integrality conditions inside $F((q))$: that $H^6\,\bar j_F^{4m}\,(\bar j_F-1728)^{3m}$ is integral over the $F$-subalgebra generated by $\bar j_F$, and that $H^2\,\bar j_F^{m}\,(\bar j_F-1728)^{m}$ is integral over the $F$-subalgebra generated by $\bar j_F^{-1}$ (the constants $1728$ being taken via the structure map of $F((q))$). The hypothesis is that the coefficientwise image `coeffMap (algebraMap K₀ K) G` of $G$ in $K((q))$ satisfies `IsModPFormFn K m`. The conclusion is that $G$ itself satisfies `IsModPFormFn K₀ m`, i.e. the two integrality conditions already hold over $K_0$.
--
--   This is the descent direction of the invariance of the integrality condition defining holomorphic mod-$p$ modular functions of weight $2m$ under base change of the coefficient field, the hypothesis of algebraicity being what makes the descent possible; the pushforward direction requires no such hypothesis. It is used in the constructions producing such functions with prescribed $q$-expansions and in the dimension estimate for linearly independent families over the rationals.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_IsModPFormFn_of_coeffMap_algebraMap.lean

